  "content": {
    "title": "Tulum Beach (2026) - All You MUST Know Before You Go (with Reviews)",
    "text": "We are travelling for 11 months and set nearly 2 months aside for Mexico. So many beautiful things to do and see but Tulum is just a theme park that at a time would have been attractive, but now, more often than not the beaches are full of the seaweed you have heard about, so those beautiful blue water pics you’ve seen are now few and far between. The Tulum ruins were the least impressive I’ve seen, Stick a few flags with holes next to them, it would make a fun golf course. Harsh but fair and my wife loves history and old castles and ruins and though she can’t bring herself to say it, she agreed that you would loose nothing if you skipped seeing it.The cenotes are different and expensive but you will see beautiful ones, but it’s not enough for me to say it made Tulum a must see, and the prices the place has grown to expect for anything you want to see or do was the icing on a cake I could live with out. Sorry Tulum but of the many spots that your beautiful country has to offer, you trail by a long way, along side of Merida which is a great base point for seeing Uxmal but that’s it.Your seaweed problem is unfortunate and can’t be helped, but you can pull back on bleeding tourists at every turn, and tone down the theme park ambiance… but hey,.. if you love that vibe than come on down and enjoy what it has to offer!",
    "word_count": 260,
    "extraction_method": "readability"
  },
